---
import DocsLayout from '../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import '../styles/pages/releases.css';
---

<DocsLayout title="Release Notes" sectionLabel="Releases" activeSlug="releases">

  <section class="section">
    <span class="section-label">Changelog</span>
    <h2>Release Notes</h2>
    <p>All notable changes to VibeCrew, following <a href="https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.1.0/">Keep a Changelog</a> and <a href="https://semver.org/spec/v2.0.0.html">Semantic Versioning</a>.</p>
  </section>

  <div class="version-nav">
    <a href="#v1.1.0" class="latest">v1.1.0</a>
    <a href="#v1.0.0">v1.0.0</a>
  </div>

  <!-- ============================================================ -->
  <!-- v1.1.0                                                       -->
  <!-- ============================================================ -->
  <div class="release-section" id="v1.1.0">
    <div class="release-header">
      <span class="release-version">v1.1.0</span>
      <span class="release-date">2026-03-05</span>
      <span class="release-badge latest">Latest</span>
    </div>

    <p class="release-summary">Competitive improvements informed by cross-framework analysis of Superpowers, GSD, BMAD, Ruflo, Ralph Loop, Kiro, Spec Kit, Composio, and Claude Squad.</p>

    <div class="change-category">
      <h3><span class="change-type added">Session 1 &mdash; Agent Prompts, Templates &amp; Scripts</span></h3>
    </div>

    <div class="feature-group">
      <h4>A1: Centralized Agent Helpers</h4>
      <ul class="file-list">
        <li>New <code>agents/helpers.md</code> with named anchors for shared procedures (register, deregister, profile, state, budget, escalation)</li>
        <li>All agents reference helpers instead of duplicating instructions &mdash; 70-85% token savings on repeated patterns</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="feature-group">
      <h4>A2: Pre-Execution Plan Verification Loop</h4>
      <ul class="file-list">
        <li>Builder validates plans against 4 criteria before execution: goal coverage, dependency integrity, context budget, EARS compliance</li>
        <li>Max 3 iterations to fix gaps, then proceeds with warnings</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="feature-group">
      <h4>A3: TDD Rationalization Resistance</h4>
      <ul class="file-list">
        <li>Structured resistance tables in TDD prompts that counter common excuses for skipping tests</li>
        <li>Integrated into Builder and Verifier agent prompts</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="feature-group">
      <h4>A4: EARS-Format Acceptance Criteria</h4>
      <ul class="file-list">
        <li>Plan template uses Easy Approach to Requirements Syntax for testable acceptance criteria</li>
        <li>Five patterns: Ubiquitous, Event-driven, State-driven, Unwanted, Optional</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="feature-group">
      <h4>A5: Status-Driven &ldquo;What Next?&rdquo;</h4>
      <ul class="file-list">
        <li><code>/status</code> now suggests the most appropriate next action based on current project state</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="change-category">
      <h3><span class="change-type added">Session 2 &mdash; Workflow &amp; Safety Enhancements</span></h3>
    </div>

    <div class="feature-group">
      <h4>B1: Discuss Phase with Decision Taxonomy</h4>
      <ul class="file-list">
        <li>New Discuss phase between Plan and Code with three decision categories: Locked, Deferred, and Discretion</li>
        <li>Locked decisions must be followed exactly; Deferred get <code>TODO(deferred)</code> comments; Discretion choices are documented with rationale</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="feature-group">
      <h4>B2: PostToolUse Context Monitoring</h4>
      <ul class="file-list">
        <li>Debounced context monitoring hook fires every 5th tool use with warnings at 45%, 60%, and 80% thresholds</li>
        <li>Complements the existing Stop hook for continuous protection against context exhaustion</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="feature-group">
      <h4>B3: Pause &amp; Resume with Worktree Cleanup</h4>
      <ul class="file-list">
        <li><code>/pause</code> commits WIP, creates handoff, stores paused state; <code>/resume</code> restores from preserved branch</li>
        <li>Clean worktree lifecycle management prevents orphaned branches</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="feature-group">
      <h4>B4: Pre-Execution Test Coverage Mapping</h4>
      <ul class="file-list">
        <li>Nyquist-pattern mapping of existing test coverage to acceptance criteria before code is written</li>
        <li>Generates Wave 0 test scaffolding tasks for uncovered criteria</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="change-category">
      <h3><span class="change-type added">Session 3 &mdash; Agent Intelligence &amp; Parallel Execution</span></h3>
    </div>

    <div class="feature-group">
      <h4>C1: Per-Agent Persistent Memory</h4>
      <ul class="file-list">
        <li>JSONL-based memory in <code>.vibecrew/memory/&lt;agent&gt;/&lt;domain&gt;.jsonl</code> with TTL-based auto-pruning</li>
        <li>Agents accumulate patterns, preferences, and lessons across sessions without bloating CLAUDE.md</li>
        <li>Enforces 50-entry and 100KB limits per domain with duplicate detection</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="feature-group">
      <h4>C2: Agent Overlay Customization</h4>
      <ul class="file-list">
        <li>Per-project agent overrides in <code>.vibecrew/agent-overrides/&lt;agent&gt;.md</code> survive plugin updates</li>
        <li>Section-matching merge: matching headings replace, new headings append, frontmatter preserved</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="feature-group">
      <h4>C3: Intent-Based Skill Triggering</h4>
      <ul class="file-list">
        <li>Natural language pattern matching maps user intent to all slash commands</li>
        <li>Session Startup agent detects intent from conversation and suggests the right skill</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="feature-group">
      <h4>C4: Parallel Backlog Execution</h4>
      <ul class="file-list">
        <li><code>/run-backlog --parallel</code> analyzes feature dependencies and groups independent features into waves</li>
        <li>Features within a wave execute simultaneously in separate Agent contexts and worktrees</li>
        <li>Topological sort respects <code>depends_on</code> relationships; circular dependencies handled gracefully</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ============================================================ -->
  <!-- v1.0.0                                                       -->
  <!-- ============================================================ -->
  <div class="release-section" id="v1.0.0">
    <div class="release-header">
      <span class="release-version">v1.0.0</span>
      <span class="release-date">2026-03-05</span>
      <a href="https://github.com/fabkrum/vibe-crew/releases/tag/v1.0.0" class="release-badge latest">GitHub Release</a>
    </div>

    <p class="release-summary">The first stable release of VibeCrew &mdash; a Claude Code plugin that transforms Claude Code into an autonomous vibe-coding operating system.</p>

    <div class="change-category">
      <h3><span class="change-type added">Highlights</span></h3>
    </div>

    <div class="feature-group">
      <h4>Two-Tier Workflow</h4>
      <ul class="file-list">
        <li><strong>Tier 1 (Project Foundation)</strong> &mdash; Sequential process creating VISION.md, design system, TDR, architecture diagrams, roadmap, and CLAUDE.md before any source code can be written</li>
        <li><strong>Tier 2 (Feature Development)</strong> &mdash; Iterative 6-phase cycle (Plan &rarr; UI Design &rarr; Code &rarr; Test &rarr; Review &rarr; Docs) for each feature</li>
        <li>Phase gate hook enforces planning before coding &mdash; no source code writes until foundation is complete</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="feature-group">
      <h4>Specialized AI Agents</h4>
      <ul class="file-list">
        <li>Opus agents for planning, research, code, security, and analysis &mdash; tasks where mistakes are expensive</li>
        <li>Haiku agents for fast, mechanical tasks like routing and running shell commands</li>
        <li>Sonnet agent for template-driven documentation output</li>
        <li>Worktree isolation for heavy research, review, and evaluation &mdash; keeps your main session fast</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="feature-group">
      <h4>Lifecycle Hooks</h4>
      <ul class="file-list">
        <li>Zero-token bash scripts enforce safety, quality gates, phase ordering, and path restrictions</li>
        <li>Quality gate runs typecheck, lint, and build on every task completion</li>
        <li>Context usage warnings at 45% and 60% to prevent slowdowns</li>
        <li>Cost guardrails with session and daily tracking against thresholds</li>
        <li>Auto-formatting of written files via PostToolUse hook</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="feature-group">
      <h4>Slash Commands</h4>
      <ul class="file-list">
        <li><strong>Setup &amp; onboarding</strong> &mdash; <code>/setup</code>, <code>/new-project</code>, <code>/onboard</code>, <code>/profile</code></li>
        <li><strong>Planning</strong> &mdash; <code>/plan-features</code>, <code>/idea</code>, <code>/status</code>, <code>/sync-issues</code></li>
        <li><strong>Development</strong> &mdash; <code>/new-feature</code>, <code>/run-backlog</code>, <code>/check</code>, <code>/debug</code>, <code>/fix-issue</code></li>
        <li><strong>Testing &amp; review</strong> &mdash; <code>/review</code>, <code>/tdd</code>, <code>/e2e</code>, <code>/perf-test</code>, <code>/a11y</code></li>
        <li><strong>Quality &amp; analysis</strong> &mdash; <code>/simplify</code>, <code>/apply-simplifications</code>, <code>/reconsider</code>, <code>/replay</code>, <code>/system-review</code></li>
        <li><strong>Safety</strong> &mdash; <code>/audit</code>, <code>/heal</code>, <code>/cost</code>, <code>/undo</code></li>
        <li><strong>Session management</strong> &mdash; <code>/wrap</code>, <code>/handoff</code>, <code>/release</code>, <code>/recover-state</code></li>
        <li><strong>Gamification</strong> &mdash; <code>/achievements</code>, <code>/quiz</code></li>
        <li><strong>Utilities</strong> &mdash; <code>/quick</code>, <code>/install-skill</code></li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="feature-group">
      <h4>MCP Servers</h4>
      <ul class="file-list">
        <li>Bundled servers for library docs (Context7), browser testing (Playwright, Chrome DevTools), and more</li>
        <li>Registry of additional servers auto-discovered and injected based on TDR technology choices</li>
        <li>Conditional activation &mdash; Semgrep, Sentry, Supabase, Stripe, Vercel, and Figma enabled from TDR</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="feature-group">
      <h4>Planning Workflow</h4>
      <ul class="file-list">
        <li><strong>Implementation plan files</strong> &mdash; Builder writes <code>docs/features/&lbrace;name&rbrace;/plan.md</code> with structured tasks (Files/Action/Verify/Done) before coding</li>
        <li><strong>Clarify sub-step</strong> &mdash; Resolves spec ambiguities before Design phase, checking 6 categories of gray areas</li>
        <li><strong>ASCII wireframes</strong> &mdash; Visual layout mockups generated during Design Phase for cheap iteration before code</li>
        <li><strong>Complexity classification</strong> &mdash; Features classified as trivial/standard/complex; trivial skips Design and Review, complex enables milestone decomposition</li>
        <li><strong>Milestone waves</strong> &mdash; Complex features broken into milestones with dependency analysis and parallel execution of independent milestones</li>
        <li><strong>Plan staleness detection</strong> &mdash; Checks if codebase changed since plan was written; auto-refreshes affected tasks</li>
        <li><strong>Plan revision tracking</strong> &mdash; Counter in state.json warns after 2+ spec changes mid-feature</li>
        <li><strong><code>/quick</code> command</strong> &mdash; Rapid single-feature execution for small tasks, skipping full backlog workflow</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="feature-group">
      <h4>Companion Skills</h4>
      <ul class="file-list">
        <li><strong>Curated registry</strong> &mdash; 6 pre-vetted skills from Anthropic, Vercel, Supabase, Cloudflare, and Stripe matched against TDR technology choices</li>
        <li><strong>Two-tier discovery</strong> &mdash; Registry match for known skills, then skills.sh search for unmatched technologies (Anthropic &rarr; vendor &rarr; community priority)</li>
        <li><strong>5-gate quality check</strong> &mdash; Trusted author, repo health, SKILL.md scan, dangerous pattern detection, and script audit before recommending discovered skills</li>
        <li><strong><code>/install-skill</code> command</strong> &mdash; Manual installation from GitHub repos, local paths, or company-internal repositories</li>
        <li><strong>Builder adaptation</strong> &mdash; When Anthropic's <code>frontend-design</code> skill is detected, Builder defers aesthetic choices to the skill</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="feature-group">
      <h4>Agent Observability</h4>
      <ul class="file-list">
        <li><strong>Agent identity system</strong> &mdash; <code>register-agent.sh</code> / <code>deregister-agent.sh</code> for lifecycle tracking with PID, session, and timestamp</li>
        <li><strong>JSONL event logging</strong> &mdash; Structured log entries for agent registration, phase completion, errors, and performance metrics</li>
        <li><strong>Session metrics</strong> &mdash; Duration, token usage, cost, cache hit rates, and tool call counts per agent session</li>
        <li><strong>Self-improvement pipeline</strong> &mdash; Performance Coach analyzes observability data to propose CLAUDE.md rule mutations</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="feature-group">
      <h4>Expertise System</h4>
      <ul class="file-list">
        <li><strong>Structured expertise records</strong> &mdash; Persist conventions, decisions, and failure patterns across sessions</li>
        <li><strong>Drift detection</strong> &mdash; Tracks when codebase conventions diverge from recorded expertise</li>
        <li><strong>Erosion tracking</strong> &mdash; Monitors degradation of code quality patterns over time</li>
        <li><strong>Expertise priming</strong> &mdash; Agents load relevant expertise records before each phase via <code>expertise-prime.sh</code></li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="feature-group">
      <h4>Testing Infrastructure</h4>
      <ul class="file-list">
        <li><strong>BATS test suite</strong> &mdash; Comprehensive unit and integration test suites with CI/CD on GitHub Actions</li>
        <li><strong>Regression test generator</strong> &mdash; Auto-generates test cases from bug fixes to prevent regressions</li>
        <li><strong>Test helpers</strong> &mdash; Isolated temp projects, state fixture builders, command mocking, and hook input constructors</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="feature-group">
      <h4>Codebase Onboarding</h4>
      <ul class="file-list">
        <li><strong>Persistent analysis</strong> &mdash; <code>/onboard</code> produces 4 analysis docs (conventions, stack, architecture, patterns) that persist across sessions</li>
        <li><strong>Analysis injection</strong> &mdash; Builder loads analysis docs before planning to skip re-discovering project conventions</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="feature-group">
      <h4>Personalization</h4>
      <ul class="file-list">
        <li>Multi-dimension user profiles: code literacy, autonomy, PR review style, verbosity, gamification preference, learning mode, and risk tolerance</li>
        <li>Every agent reads the profile and adapts behavior to your experience level and preferences</li>
        <li>Preset selection or guided interview via <code>/profile</code></li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="feature-group">
      <h4>Gamification &amp; Vibe Score</h4>
      <ul class="file-list">
        <li>Vibe Score quality rating per session (0&ndash;130) measuring prompt efficiency, test coverage, documentation freshness, and workflow compliance</li>
        <li>XP, leveling, badges, skill trees, streaks, and challenges that reward good development habits</li>
        <li>Performance Coach proposes permanent CLAUDE.md rule mutations based on anti-pattern detection</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="feature-group">
      <h4>Status Line</h4>
      <ul class="file-list">
        <li>Persistent terminal status bar showing model, context usage, cost, active feature and phase, Vibe Score, and compaction count</li>
        <li>Updates after every assistant message at zero token cost</li>
        <li>Graceful degradation when dependencies are missing</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="feature-group">
      <h4>Vibe Dashboard</h4>
      <ul class="file-list">
        <li>Browser-based VitePress dashboard with Kanban board, score trends, achievements, and settings</li>
        <li>Architecture overview rendering Mermaid diagrams from <code>.vibecrew/architecture/*.mmd</code></li>
        <li>Live session data via atomic JSON writes from the status line script</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="feature-group">
      <h4>Design Discovery</h4>
      <ul class="file-list">
        <li>3-phase interview: Product &amp; Audience Context &rarr; Visual Direction &rarr; Component Preferences</li>
        <li>Bring-your-own design system: import from CSS, Tailwind, JSON tokens, URL, Figma, or brand PDF</li>
        <li>Both paths produce identical output: <code>design-system.css</code> + <code>design-brief.md</code></li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="feature-group">
      <h4>Safety &amp; Security</h4>
      <ul class="file-list">
        <li>Permission rules with allowed and denied tool patterns</li>
        <li>Dangerous command protection (rm -rf, DROP TABLE, force push)</li>
        <li>Path restriction to project root</li>
        <li>OWASP Top 10 security auditing via <code>/audit</code></li>
        <li>CI failure diagnosis and repair via <code>/heal</code> (max 3 attempts)</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="feature-group">
      <h4>Cross-Session State</h4>
      <ul class="file-list">
        <li><code>.vibecrew/</code> directory with JSON state files, session logs, scores, signals, locks, and handoffs</li>
        <li>Cross-session context transfer via <code>/handoff</code></li>
        <li>Cross-project telemetry with anonymized performance data for <code>/system-review</code></li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="feature-group">
      <h4>Documentation</h4>
      <ul class="file-list">
        <li>Companion docs site built with Astro, self-hosted fonts, dark/light theme, and Pagefind search</li>
        <li>Setup guides, workflow walkthroughs, architecture reference, glossary, and FAQ</li>
        <li>Auto-generated docs via Doc Generator agent during <code>/wrap</code></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

</DocsLayout>
